# File: scripts/__tests__/delivery-pull-request-body.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/597-delivery-pr-body-copies-verification-report-headings-into-the-verification-section-and-drops-the-changed-path-evidence/requirements.md
Feature: Delivery PR body keeps report headings out of the Verification section

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A report heading is not copied into the body
    Given a verification report with the heading "### Review Findings (all `info`, carried from the passed review)"
    When the delivery pull-request body is built
    Then the body contains no line from the report that starts a Markdown heading

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: The changed-path list stays verification evidence
    Given that report and changed paths "VERSION", "package.json" and ".claude-plugin/plugin.json"
    When the built body is evaluated by the contribution evidence check
    Then every changed path is matched and the evaluation passes

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Command results are still copied
    Given a verification report with the line <line>
    When the delivery pull-request body is built
    Then that line appears in the Verification section before "Changed paths:"

    Examples:
      | line                                   |
      | "- `npm test` — passed"                |
      | "\| `git diff --check` \| Pass \|"     |
